	(text "# Design Constraints\n## Input Voltage\n- vehicle running: ~14.4V\n- vehicle off, battery only : ~12V\n- transients like load dump 35V maybe\n## Current Supply\n- powered off of the trailer connector on a vehicle: often protected with a 10 or 20 amp fuse, safe design limit closer to 5 to 7.5A continuous draw\n## Light Output Targets\n- probably liek 700lm is sufficient, 1500lm too much, maybe like 800-1200 target\n   - also note a well-focused 800lm light will way outperform a 1500lm light spreading light where its unwanted"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 163.576 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "233003df-60f9-4356-a305-a85eddaf9ea3")
	)
	(text "- Mounting Holes for license plate holder screws"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.256 87.884 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3302e575-a963-44ee-af31-f0a560d63034")
	)
	(text "# LED Brightness Calculation\n\n- LED brightness (relative luminous flux) is directly proportional to Forward Current\n\n- I_led = V_led_string / R\n- I_led = (V_vehicle - 3 * V_led_f) / R\n\n## Max\n\n- I_led_max = (V_vehicle_max - 3 * V_led_f) / R\n- I_led_max = (16 - 3 * 2.67) / 100\n- I_led_max = 79.9mA\n\n## Min\n\n- I_led_min = (V_vehicle_min - 3 * V_led_f) / R\n- I_led_min = (10 - 3 * 2.67) / 100\n- I_led_min = 19.9mA\n\n# LED Specifications\n\n- typical flux: 33lm\n- forward current max: 480mA\n- forward current target: 100mA\n   - target chosen for long lifespan and brightness and heat dissipation\n- 55mA is 100% flux\n\n# Total String Brightness\n\n- if all at 55mA\n    - 33lm * 3 * 8\n    - 792lm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 122.428 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "3ff377ee-e8aa-4423-8d34-874b4be51ebb")
	)
	(text "- bulk capacitance 100u\n- slight filtering with a 1u and 100n\n- TVS for general transiets, clamp above 35V load dump\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 22.352 43.688 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4b2c281a-dbdf-43ca-bac9-b2f9d5aa621a")
	)
	(text "# Design Choices\n## Emitter\n- Cree JB2835BWT-F-H40EA0000-N000P001\n   - Vf: 2.7V (good, can easily get 3 in series from a 12V nominal supply)\n   - Viewing angle: 120 (good, fairly wide flood spread)\n   - CCT: 4000k (maybe a bit yellow but at least not blindingly blue)\n   - flux: 40lm (like 24 gets 960 lumens, good)\n   - CRI: 80 (not the best but at least it's not total garbage at like 60 or 70, probably a really good CRI for the price especiialy)\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.558 186.944 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dd5dd9e1-64bb-422e-b547-d0f36865718f")
	)
